# drokk-ffmpeg — pinned upstream sources.
#
# This file is the single source of truth for what goes into a drokk-ffmpeg
# binary. Together with configure-flags.sh and the two build scripts it is the
# complete recipe: that is what discharges the GPL "corresponding source"
# obligation for the ffmpeg.exe / ffmpeg the DrokkPuppet mods ship.
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE, '#' comments. Both the tag AND the peeled commit are
# recorded. The build scripts clone --depth 1 --branch <tag> and then assert
# `git rev-parse HEAD` equals the commit; a tag that moves is caught, not
# silently accepted.
#
# Verified with `git ls-remote` on 2026-09-03.

# --- ffmpeg -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Newest stable release tag of the n8.1 series (n8.1, n8.1.1, n8.1.2 exist; no
# n8.2). Matches the ffmpeg Fedora 44 ships, which is a useful sanity check.
# NOTE: this is the PEELED commit (`n8.1.2^{}`), i.e. what a --branch clone
# leaves at HEAD -- NOT the annotated tag object (1c2c67c0...).
FFMPEG_REPO=https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg.git
FFMPEG_TAG=n8.1.2
FFMPEG_COMMIT=38b88335f99e76ed89ff3c93f877fdefce736c13

# --- x264 -------------------------------------------------------------------
# x264 publishes NO tags at all (`git ls-remote --tags` returns nothing), so a
# raw commit off a named branch is the only possible pin. We track `stable`,
# which is the branch distributions track.
X264_REPO=https://code.videolan.org/videolan/x264.git
X264_BRANCH=stable
X264_COMMIT=b35605ace3ddf7c1a5d67a2eb553f034aef41d55
# For reference, master as of the same ls-remote:
#   0480cb05fa188d37ae87e8f4fd8f1aea3711f7ee

# --- nv-codec-headers (ffnvcodec) -------------------------------------------
# Header-only. Enables h264_nvenc, which 7 Days to Die's video path REQUIRES
# (it hardcodes -c:v h264_nvenc with no libx264 fallback).
#
# PIN THE OLDEST VERSION FFMPEG ACCEPTS, NOT THE NEWEST THAT EXISTS. These
# headers declare an NVENC API version and the driver refuses anything newer
# than it implements. Built against n13.1.15.0 (the newest tag), h264_nvenc
# died at runtime on an RTX 3090 with:
#     Driver does not support the required nvenc API version.
#     Required: 13.1 Found: 13.0
#     The minimum required Nvidia driver for nvenc is 610.00 or newer
# -- i.e. the newest headers silently raise the driver floor for every player.
# ffmpeg n8.1.2's configure floor is `ffnvcodec >= 12.1.14.0` (configure:7126),
# so n12.1.14.1 is the most compatible pin that still configures: NVENC SDK
# 12.1, driver >= 531.61 (Windows) / 530.41 (Linux), March 2023.
NVCODEC_REPO=https://github.com/FFmpeg/nv-codec-headers.git
NVCODEC_TAG=n12.1.14.1
NVCODEC_COMMIT=7c8e7fc751f803c672b42c37d9199c8a4f98b327

# --- opus -------------------------------------------------------------------
# BSD-3-Clause. Used by the Lethal Company and 7 Days audio pipes
# (-c:a libopus). Built from source rather than taken from the distro so the
# Windows and Linux binaries have identical composition.
OPUS_REPO=https://github.com/xiph/opus.git
OPUS_TAG=v1.5.2
OPUS_COMMIT=ddbe48383984d56acd9e1ab6a090c54ca6b735a6
